[{"id":3834705942,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7kkPgW","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally on https://github.com/Calinou/godot-reflection, it mostly works as expected.\r\n\r\nForward+ | Mobile | Compatibility\r\n-|-|-\r\n<img width=\"1036\" height=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc789443-2833-4309-b51d-f3c46b4405ae\" /> | <img width=\"1036\" height=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f285c546-dea8-4fa1-893c-05bbf47be6ac\" /> | <img width=\"1036\" height=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86c96b92-fce2-4c0a-99bc-238ce6bee259\" />\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- Having glow enabled in Compatibility makes the view much brighter.\r\n  Having SSAO enabled in Compatibility also makes the view darker.\r\n  When either of these effects are enabled, changing the tonemap mode will also affect the debug view.\r\n\r\nGlow + SSAO | Glow | Nothing\r\n-|-|-\r\n<img width=\"1036\" height=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86c96b92-fce2-4c0a-99bc-238ce6bee259\" /> | <img width=\"1036\" height=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4f68e394-4ec6-458d-9bd9-d443c6f0c8aa\" /> | <img width=\"1036\" height=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64cc13cf-885f-47ee-a732-22e791e67de4\" />\r\n\r\n- In Compatibility, if you increase the camera's Near value by a wide margin (I used `5.0` here), SSAO becomes visible in the debug view:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1036\" height=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c814499c-872f-475a-803f-37d1b28948e2\" />\r\n\r\nIn general, tonemapping and effects should be skipped while in the normal/depth debug draw modes, as they don't affect the result and just take up GPU time. The effects aren't visible in Forward+/Mobile, but they are still being processed (this can be seen by looking at the frame time display when changing debug draw modes).","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116446#pullrequestreview-3834705942","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116446","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116446#pullrequestreview-3834705942"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116446"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-21T00:25:15Z","commit_id":null}]